\section{Precision}{

Results are doubles. Stata's default storage type for new variables is
\code{float} (see \verb{set type}), and \code{egen} without an explicit type is assumed
to follow it. A \code{float} holds integers exactly only up to 16,777,216, so
16,777,217 cannot be stored and becomes 16,777,216. \code{stata_rowtotal()}
gives 16,777,217, which corresponds to
\verb{egen double t = rowtotal(a b)}. Totals of Rupiah amounts and other
large values can therefore differ from Stata output created without
\code{double}. statacompat does not emulate \code{float} storage.
}

